    "table": {
      "session_id": "chat-b1a1c010bb4e45d4bcf14449c1a202a0",
      "answer": "As of **2026-10-16**, the wells below are classified as **not producing** from their latest inspections. Each has a temperature rise below the T200 production threshold of **15°C above ambient** (fleet/well-types/T200.md, §9.3).\n\n- **WELL-0164:** Pump jack observed not moving; the underlying cause is not recorded (INS-0164-0205).\n- **WELL-0170:** Open repair for walking-beam bearing wear (MNT-0170-031; INS-0170-0206).\n- **WELL-0172:** No stroke observed; an open repair also records a flowline corrosion pinhole leak (INS-0172-0206; MNT-0172-028). The records do not explicitly establish which caused the current stoppage.\n- **WELL-0175:** Low temperature rise indicates non-production, but no explanatory note or open repair is recorded (INS-0175-0204).\n\nThe recorded administrative status remains **active** for WELL-0164, WELL-0172 and WELL-0175 despite the inspection-based non-production finding. No additional context reason is recorded for these wells.",
